{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-79fd14fa-95ba-40f2-86f5-cb2b1db41a29","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a40425bb4519c069","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9014-4razyxl3/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9014-E001.md","content":"# Llama Stack GA-readiness assessment and definitive GA scope\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic resolves the strategy's central unknown: the full inventory of gaps\nbetween Llama Stack's current Tech Preview quality and the General\nAvailability bar. TP feedback is scattered across support tickets and no\nsystematic GA-readiness assessment has been done. This investigation\nconsolidates that feedback with a technical audit of the distribution and\nproduces the definitive GA scope that all stability, hardening, and support\nposture work is planned against.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Collect and consolidate TP feedback from the support ticket corpus and other\n  feedback channels (issues, escalations, field reports).\n- Audit the current distribution against the four GA-bar inventory areas named\n  by the strategy:\n  - **API stability** — current API surface state, versioning posture, and\n    stability risks on the OpenAI-compatible REST APIs and the\n    LlamaStackDistribution CRD.\n  - **Upgrade paths** — what upgrades between TP releases currently work,\n    break, or are untested.\n  - **Scale limits** — characterize current known limits (or explicitly mark\n    them unknown) for the distribution at production-representative scale.\n  - **Error handling** — audit error surfaces, failure modes, and observability\n    of failures against the GA bar.\n- Classify each identified gap as GA-blocking or non-blocking, with severity\n  and owning area.\n- Produce the **definitive GA scope document**: which gaps are in scope for\n  GA, which are deferred with rationale, and the resulting size estimate for\n  the stability and hardening work.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A gap inventory exists that covers all four inventory areas (API stability,\n  upgrade paths, scale limits, error handling), with each gap classified\n  (GA-blocking / non-blocking), severity-assigned, and traceable to evidence\n  (ticket, test result, or code audit finding).\n- The TP feedback corpus has been systematically reviewed, not sampled; the\n  inventory states the corpus coverage.\n- Scale limits are characterized with measured or evidence-backed values, or\n  explicitly marked unknown with a characterization plan.\n- A definitive GA scope document is published that states which gaps are in\n  GA scope, which are deferred with rationale, and the resulting scope for\n  the stability, hardening, and support-posture work.\n- The GA scope document is delivered to the strategy stakeholders for\n  acceptance.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)**: GA-readiness assessment inventories the gaps between\n  current TP quality and GA bar (API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits,\n  error handling), producing the definitive GA scope — this epic is the full\n  delivery of HLR-1.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":34447,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-851ecc90abcf5800","agent_id":"a3644c9c9ed43a63e","session_id":"71dcbc61-9434-456e-a363-a4d82acc6903","uuid":"efde316b-3c7a-4b73-a9a3-102f51f571c1","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:16:50.466Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014 into epics"}
