{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aab3cf7f7a4a8b11","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n3\ttitle: Llama Stack GA-readiness assessment and definitive GA scope\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 1\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Llama Stack GA-readiness assessment and definitive GA scope\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis epic resolves the strategy's central unknown: the full inventory of gaps\n30\tbetween Llama Stack's current Tech Preview quality and the General\n31\tAvailability bar. TP feedback is scattered across support tickets and no\n32\tsystematic GA-readiness assessment has been done. This investigation\n33\tconsolidates that feedback with a technical audit of the distribution and\n34\tproduces the definitive GA scope that all stability, hardening, and support\n35\tposture work is planned against.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Collect and consolidate TP feedback from the support ticket corpus and other\n40\t  feedback channels (issues, escalations, field reports).\n41\t- Audit the current distribution against the four GA-bar inventory areas named\n42\t  by the strategy:\n43\t  - **API stability** — current API surface state, versioning posture, and\n44\t    stability risks on the OpenAI-compatible REST APIs and the\n45\t    LlamaStackDistribution CRD.\n46\t  - **Upgrade paths** — what upgrades between TP releases currently work,\n47\t    break, or are untested.\n48\t  - **Scale limits** — characterize current known limits (or explicitly mark\n49\t    them unknown) for the distribution at production-representative scale.\n50\t  - **Error handling** — audit error surfaces, failure modes, and observability\n51\t    of failures against the GA bar.\n52\t- Classify each identified gap as GA-blocking or non-blocking, with severity\n53\t  and owning area.\n54\t- Produce the **definitive GA scope document**: which gaps are in scope for\n55\t  GA, which are deferred with rationale, and the resulting size estimate for\n56\t  the stability and hardening work.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- A gap inventory exists that covers all four inventory areas (API stability,\n61\t  upgrade paths, scale limits, error handling), with each gap classified\n62\t  (GA-blocking / non-blocking), severity-assigned, and traceable to evidence\n63\t  (ticket, test result, or code audit finding).\n64\t- The TP feedback corpus has been systematically reviewed, not sampled; the\n65\t  inventory states the corpus coverage.\n66\t- Scale limits are characterized with measured or evidence-backed values, or\n67\t  explicitly marked unknown with a characterization plan.\n68\t- A definitive GA scope document is published that states which gaps are in\n69\t  GA scope, which are deferred with rationale, and the resulting scope for\n70\t  the stability, hardening, and support-posture work.\n71\t- The GA scope document is delivered to the strategy stakeholders for\n72\t  acceptance.\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability\n75\t\n76\t- **HLR-1 (P0)**: GA-readiness assessment inventories the gaps between\n77\t  current TP quality and GA bar (API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits,\n78\t  error handling), producing the definitive GA scope — this epic is the full\n79\t  delivery of HLR-1.\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-98b340ca48b046e4","agent_id":"a8981028e057760d0","session_id":"71dcbc61-9434-456e-a363-a4d82acc6903","uuid":"e3d7b069-6a20-4acd-bfef-231b499817b7","timest