{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9fbda76e90475441","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E002\n3\ttitle: Llama Stack API stability guarantee and GA hardening\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the GA-readiness assessment finds the gap inventory materially\n15\t    larger or different than estimated, rewrite this epic's scope from the assessment's\n16\t    definitive GA scope; remediation items may be split into separate hardening epics\n17\t    by area.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: -1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Medium\n31\tai_implementability_score: 2\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Llama Stack API stability guarantee and GA hardening\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tThis epic delivers the published API stability guarantee for Llama Stack's GA\n40\tsurface and closes the quality gaps the GA-readiness assessment identifies.\n41\tIt takes the distribution from \"quality gaps excused by Tech Preview status\"\n42\tto the GA bar on the same surface: versioned APIs, a deprecation policy, a\n43\ttested upgrade path from the last two TP releases, and remediation of the\n44\tGA-blocking gaps in error handling and other assessment-identified areas.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Version the published API surface (OpenAI-compatible REST APIs and the\n49\t  LlamaStackDistribution CRD) so GA consumers can pin against stable versions.\n50\t- Author and publish a deprecation policy covering the GA API surface.\n51\t- Build and test the upgrade path from the last two TP releases to the GA\n52\t  version, preserving distribution configuration and state across upgrades.\n53\t- Close GA-blocking quality gaps identified by the readiness assessment\n54\t  (error handling and the other inventory areas), or get them explicitly\n55\t  deferred with rationale in the GA scope.\n56\t- Fold the TP-feedback remediation items that the assessment places in GA\n57\t  scope into this hardening pass over the distribution.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- The published GA API surface is versioned, and a deprecation policy document\n62\t  covering that surface is published.\n63\t- Upgrade from each of the last two TP releases to the GA version is tested,\n64\t  with test evidence that distribution configuration and state are preserved;\n65\t  failures are fixed or the incompatibility is documented in the migration\n66\t  notes with a workaround.\n67\t- Every GA-blocking gap in the assessment's inventory is closed or explicitly\n68\t  deferred with rationale recorded against the GA scope.\n69\t- Error handling on the distribution meets the GA bar as characterized by the\n70\t  readiness assessment.\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- **HLR-2 (P0)**: published API surface carries a stability guarantee —\n75\t  versioned APIs, deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from the last\n76\t  two TP releases — delivered by this epic.\n77\t- Assessed gap-closure scope from HLR-1's inventory is absorbed here as one\n78\t  hardening pass over the same distribution surface.\n79\t\n80\t## Risks / Notes\n81\t\n82\t- Scope is an estimate until the GA-readiness assessment lands; this epic is\n83\t  gated on that assessment and its scope is rewritten by its findings.\n84\t- Re-split trigger: if the assessment's gap inventory exceeds the\n85\t  stability-mechanics work in volume, split the remediation items into\n86\t  separate hardening epics by area.\n87\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-98b340ca48b046e4","agent_id":"a8981028e057760d0","session_id":"71dcbc61-9434-456e-a363-a4d82acc6903","uuid":"53b01ea1-d689-41c2-a741-010943a3efa1","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:20:45.665Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9fbda76e90475441","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
