{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-989b82622484a7ce","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E005\n3\ttitle: TrustyAI validation of the guardrails integration for GA distributions\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9014-E004\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 5\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# TrustyAI validation of the guardrails integration for GA distributions\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic is the TrustyAI team's validation of the TrustyAI guardrails\n35\tintegration with Llama Stack GA distributions. TrustyAI itself is already a\n36\tGA component and requires no code changes for this strategy; its role is to\n37\tvalidate and certify, from the TrustyAI side, that the guardrails integration\n38\tshipped in Llama Stack GA distributions is supported — functionally correct\n39\tagainst representative TrustyAI configurations, with documented compatibility\n40\tand support boundaries.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Define and run a validation suite exercising the guardrails integration\n45\t  across representative TrustyAI service configurations and Llama Stack\n46\t  distribution setups: functional behavior, configuration handling, and\n47\t  failure modes (guardrails service unavailable, misconfiguration).\n48\t- Document the TrustyAI-side compatibility and support statement for the\n49\t  integration: which TrustyAI versions/configurations are supported with GA\n50\t  distributions, and known limitations.\n51\t- File and escalate integration defects found during validation to the\n52\t  distribution owners, and re-validate fixes.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- A validation report exists covering the exercised configurations, with\n57\t  pass/fail results for functional behavior, configuration handling, and\n58\t  failure modes.\n59\t- All defects found during validation are filed against the owning teams, and\n60\t  blocking defects are resolved and re-validated.\n61\t- The TrustyAI-side compatibility and support statement for the integration\n62\t  is documented and published (supported versions/configurations, known\n63\t  limitations).\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- **HLR-4 (P1)**: safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented\n68\t  integration for GA distributions — the TrustyAI-team validation and\n69\t  support-statement half of this requirement.\n70\t\n71\t## Risks / Notes\n72\t\n73\t- This work cannot start before the distribution-side integration promotion\n74\t  is available to validate.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-98b340ca48b046e4","agent_id":"a8981028e057760d0","session_id":"71dcbc61-9434-456e-a363-a4d82acc6903","uuid":"7269a339-ffa1-4f89-9f6b-e479bdc09521","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:20:49.013Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-989b82622484a7ce","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
