1\t\n162\tEvery epic has testable ACs derived from the HLR text. Rule-mandated ACs are\n163\tpresent where applicable: E006 replaces existing opt-in behavior and carries\n164\tthe feature-flag revert AC (rollback); E007 has the \"technically reviewed\n165\tagainst the implemented GA behavior by engineering, with review evidence\n166\trecorded\" AC; no epic has a konflux-onboarding chain, so the build-pipeline AC\n167\tis N/A. No AC states an externally-controlled schedule or availability\n168\tprecondition — E001's \"delivered to the strategy stakeholders for acceptance\"\n169\tand E003's \"reviewed and accepted by the support organization\" are conditions\n170\ton deliverables the epics themselves produce (the standard completion point\n171\tfor document deliverables). No epic body references sibling epics by draft ID.\n172\t\n173\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n174\t\n175\tAll strategy scope is accounted for: the four assessment inventory areas\n176\t(E001), versioning/deprecation policy/upgrade path from the last two TP\n177\treleases (E002), SLO targets/backport policy/supported configuration matrix\n178\t(E003), guardrails promotion with supported-and-documented integration (E004 +\n179\tE005), Dashboard default-on including the non-entitled-cluster behavior (E006),\n180\tand GA documentation uplift with TP migration notes (E007, covering the\n181\tupgrade path, the Dashboard opt-in-to-default change, and formerly\n182\texperimental integrations). The strategy's open question is carried forward as\n183\tthe E001 gate rather than dropped, and the missing strategy sections (teams\n184\ttable, ACs, NFRs) are flagged as Health Warnings rather than silently ignored.\n185\tRule 19 non-application was reviewed and confirmed: HLR-4 promotes an existing\n186\tintegration with an already-GA component rather than designing a new safety\n187\tmechanism, and failure modes are exercised in E005's validation scope — the\n188\tdecomposition's flagged reading is sound. The unbounded outcome set of E001\n189\tcorrectly yields phased decomposition rather than conditional branches. The\n190\tonly completeness-adjacent defect is the E004/E007 documentation duplication\n191\trecorded under Epic Boundaries above; no strategy capability is left uncovered.\n192\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-afb136f90b8b5998","agent_id":"a8286fcc73ec88da9","session_id":"71dcbc61-9434-456e-a363-a4d82acc6903","uuid":"e7f71fac-77d7-4259-b977-0f714d8ead7e","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:25:04.510Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a91be9b723a1b0d7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
