ion, supported options, and\n50\t  behavior.\n51\t- Exercise the integration functionally (guardrails applying to distribution\n52\t  traffic, expected failure behavior when TrustyAI is unavailable) so the\n53\t  promotion is evidence-backed, in coordination with the TrustyAI team's\n54\t  validation of the integration.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- TrustyAI guardrails can be enabled on a GA Llama Stack distribution as a\n59\t  supported configuration path — no experimental flag or opt-in gate is\n60\t  required.\n61\t- The integration's configuration surface is versioned and covered by the\n62\t  distribution's deprecation policy.\n63\t- Integration documentation exists covering enablement, configuration\n64\t  options, and behavior when the guardrails service is unavailable.\n65\t- Functional evidence exists that guardrails apply to distribution traffic in\n66\t  the supported configuration, and failure modes are handled per the\n67\t  distribution's error-handling bar.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- **HLR-4 (P1)**: safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented\n72\t  integration (not an experimental flag) for GA distributions — the\n73\t  distribution-side delivery of this requirement.\n74\t\n75\t## Risks / Notes\n76\t\n77\t- Cross-team coordination with the TrustyAI team is expected for validation\n78\t  and compatibility statements; the TrustyAI team's validation effort is\n79\t  tracked as its own work item.\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-afb136f90b8b5998","agent_id":"a8286fcc73ec88da9","session_id":"71dcbc61-9434-456e-a363-a4d82acc6903","uuid":"5d713df6-f88c-4da3-9578-46c2b45c200a","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:25:15.330Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae8bcc743f05b2ca","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
