blish the supported configuration matrix: the distributions,\n52\t  providers, dependency versions, and scale envelopes that are supported at\n53\t  GA, reflecting the scale limits characterized by the GA-readiness\n54\t  assessment.\n55\t- Align the posture documents with the platform's existing GA support\n56\t  standards so Llama Stack is supportable by the standard production support\n57\t  channels.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- SLO targets for the GA distribution are documented and stated in measurable\n62\t  terms.\n63\t- The backport policy is documented, covering supported releases, fix\n64\t  selection criteria, and duration.\n65\t- The supported configuration matrix is published and reflects the scale\n66\t  limits and provider/configuration constraints validated in the\n67\t  GA-readiness assessment.\n68\t- The support posture documents are reviewed and accepted by the support\n69\t  organization and product stakeholders.\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- **HLR-3 (P0)**: production support posture in place — documented SLO\n74\t  targets, backport policy, and supported configuration matrix — delivered by\n75\t  this epic.\n76\t\n77\t## Risks / Notes\n78\t\n79\t- The supported configuration matrix portion of this epic is gated on the\n80\t  GA-readiness assessment (scale-limit characterization); SLO and backport\n81\t  policy work can proceed independently once the epic starts.\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-90be83002d9b1935","agent_id":"a552b5e19b6263c40","session_id":"71dcbc61-9434-456e-a363-a4d82acc6903","uuid":"533ec8e9-acc2-44c6-aa52-970ab6d7d268","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:28:27.215Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8b7bfd38411d888","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
