r when TrustyAI is unavailable) so the\n50\t  promotion is evidence-backed, in coordination with the TrustyAI team's\n51\t  validation of the integration.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- TrustyAI guardrails can be enabled on a GA Llama Stack distribution as a\n56\t  supported configuration path — no experimental flag or opt-in gate is\n57\t  required.\n58\t- The integration's configuration surface is versioned and covered by the\n59\t  distribution's deprecation policy.\n60\t- The promoted guardrails configuration surface — enablement steps, supported\n61\t  configuration options, and behavior when the guardrails service is\n62\t  unavailable — is handed to documentation as engineering input for the GA\n63\t  documentation uplift.\n64\t- Functional evidence exists that guardrails apply to distribution traffic in\n65\t  the supported configuration, and failure modes are handled per the\n66\t  distribution's error-handling bar.\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- **HLR-4 (P1)**: safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented\n71\t  integration (not an experimental flag) for GA distributions — this epic\n72\t  delivers the distribution-side half: the promoted, supported integration\n73\t  and its versioned configuration surface. The documented-integration half\n74\t  is delivered by the GA documentation uplift, which authors the guardrails\n75\t  configuration topic from the configuration surface this epic hands over.\n76\t\n77\t## Risks / Notes\n78\t\n79\t- Cross-team coordination with the TrustyAI team is expected for validation\n80\t  and compatibility statements; the TrustyAI team's validation effort is\n81\t  tracked as its own work item.\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-90be83002d9b1935","agent_id":"a552b5e19b6263c40","session_id":"71dcbc61-9434-456e-a363-a4d82acc6903","uuid":"a7ed32df-590f-4308-9ce8-3425f1bd2e3c","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:28:28.195Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b915c8b49b22e719","perm