ns are supported with GA\n50\t  distributions, and known limitations.\n51\t- File and escalate integration defects found during validation to the\n52\t  distribution owners, and re-validate fixes.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- A validation report exists covering the exercised configurations, with\n57\t  pass/fail results for functional behavior, configuration handling, and\n58\t  failure modes.\n59\t- All defects found during validation are filed against the owning teams, and\n60\t  blocking defects are resolved and re-validated.\n61\t- The TrustyAI-side compatibility and support statement for the integration\n62\t  is documented and published (supported versions/configurations, known\n63\t  limitations).\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- **HLR-4 (P1)**: safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented\n68\t  integration for GA distributions — the TrustyAI-team validation and\n69\t  support-statement half of this requirement.\n70\t\n71\t## Risks / Notes\n72\t\n73\t- This work cannot start before the distribution-side integration promotion\n74\t  is available to validate.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-90be83002d9b1935","agent_id":"a552b5e19b6263c40","session_id":"71dcbc61-9434-456e-a363-a4d82acc6903","uuid":"11db8d38-7934-4c3c-8ccd-2991b3e4e22d","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:28:30.702Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f76af2ea903a475","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
